     "Log a release or termination order as soon as it arrives and record the payroll cycle when withholding should stop. A release that sits in an inbox can cause an extra deduction and a refund request. Record the stop date and the person who confirmed it with payroll. The entry should show the last cycle that withheld and the first that did not.",
     "Record any competing order against the same employee and the priority question it raises. The support lane can list the orders, the dates, and the amounts, but the lawyer decides which one controls. Record the question and the instruction that follows. Do not let payroll choose a priority by default.",
     "Keep a short note on each communication with the creditor's counsel or the court clerk. Record the date, the person, and the substance of the call or message. A verbal instruction should be confirmed in writing the same day. The log is stronger when each external contact has a written trace."
