     "Record the page count and the date range of each production so a reviewer can spot an obvious gap. A production that stops before the relevant treatment date may need a follow-up. Record the apparent gap without interpreting the medical content. The lawyer or a qualified reviewer decides what the gap means.",
     "If a provider sends records for the wrong patient, record the mismatch and quarantine the file. Do not add it to the matter record and do not destroy it without instruction. Record who identified the mismatch and where the file is held. The lawyer decides the next step.",
     "Record the storage location of each production and the access list. Medical records need tighter access than a general matter folder, and the tracker should show who can open the file. Review the access list when a role changes. The record of access is part of the control."
