     "If the court identifies a missing attachment, record the item and the date the corrected filing is due. Rebuild the attachment from the source rather than editing a screenshot. Record the new version and the reviewer. The correction should be traceable to the court's notice.",
     "Keep the denied or deficient filing in the record rather than deleting it. The history shows what was submitted and what changed. Record the location and the relationship to the corrected filing. A clean file is not the same as a complete file.",
     "Notify the matter team and the client contact according to the firm's instruction after a denial. Record who was notified and what they were told. The lawyer controls the message and any next step. The support lane records the communication without characterizing the legal effect."
